#X msg 130 602 apin_mapping?;
#X text 270 602 query mapping between analog port number and digital
pin. Analog messages are numbered 0 to 15 \, which traditionally refer
to the Arduino pins labeled A0 \, A1 \, A2 \, etc. However \, these
pis are actually configured using "normal" pin numbers in the pin mode
message \, and when those pins are used for non-analog functions. The
analog mapping query provides the information about which pins (as
used with Firmata's pin mode message) correspond to the analog channels.
Return sequence of messages like: [apin_mapping A# PIN#( \, where #
is number.;
#X obj 250 763 cnv 1 515 1 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -216373 -1 0;
#X msg 130 763 capabilities?;
#X text 270 763 query pin capabilities. Return sequence of messages
like: [pin_info PIN# MODE RESOLUTION( \, where # is pin number.;
#X obj 250 818 cnv 1 515 1 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -216373 -1 0;
#X msg 130 818 firmware?;
#X text 270 818 query firmata protocol version. Returns message like:
[firmware ARDUINO_FIRMWARE_NAME.ino MAJOR MINOR(.;
#X obj 250 858 cnv 1 515 1 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -216373 -1 0;
#X msg 130 858 pin_mode;
#X text 270 858 sets pin mode. Arguments are:;
#X obj 280 881 cnv 1 37 23 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -245695 -1 0;
#X text 280 881 PIN#: pin number. Type: int. Min value: 0\.;
#X obj 280 904 cnv 1 38 23 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -245695 -1 0;
#X text 280 904 MODE: pin mode. Type: symbol. Allowed values: INPUT
\, OUTPUT \, ANALOG \, PWM \, SERVO \, SHIFT \, I2C \, ONEWIRE \, STEPPER
\, ENCODER \, SERIAL \, PULLUP.;
#X obj 250 959 cnv 1 515 1 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -216373 -1 0;
#X msg 130 959 pin_state?;
#X text 270 959 query pin state. The pin state is any data written
to the pin (it is important to note that pin state != pin value). For
output modes (digital output \, PWM \, and Servo) \, the state is any
value that has been previously written to the pin. For input modes
\, typically the state is zero. However \, for digital inputs \, the
state is the status of the pull-up resistor which is 1 if enabled \,
0 if disabled. Returns message like [pin_state PIN# MODE state( \,
where # is pin number. Arguments are:;
#X obj 280 1103 cnv 1 37 23 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -245695 -1 0;
#X text 280 1103 PIN#: pin number. Type: int.;
#X obj 250 1128 cnv 1 515 1 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -216373 -1 0;
#X msg 130 1128 report_apin;
#X text 270 1128 turns on/off analog pin (A0-A6) value reporting. Arguments
are:;
#X obj 280 1166 cnv 1 83 23 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -245695 -1 0;
#X text 280 1166 ANALOG_PIN: analog pin number. Type: int.;
#X obj 280 1189 cnv 1 45 23 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -245695 -1 0;
#X text 280 1189 VALUE: value. If 1 - activates analog reporting \,
messages like [apin PIN# value( are returned every sampling interval
(by default 19ms). Type: int. Allowed values: 0 \, 1\.;
#X obj 250 1259 cnv 1 515 1 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -216373 -1 0;
#X msg 130 1259 report_dport;
#X text 270 1259 turns on/off digital port value reporting. Arguments
are:;
#X obj 280 1282 cnv 1 45 23 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -245695 -1 0;
#X text 280 1282 PORT#: digital port number. Port is a group of pins
\, port 0 refers pins 0-8\. Type: int.;
#X obj 280 1320 cnv 1 45 23 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -245695 -1 0;
#X text 280 1320 VALUE: value. If 1 - activates digital port reporting
\, messages like [dport PORT# value( are returned only on pin value
change. Type: int. Allowed values: 0 \, 1\.;
#X obj 250 1375 cnv 1 515 1 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -216373 -1 0;
#X msg 130 1375 samp_interval;
#X text 270 1375 sets sampling interval - how often analog data and
i2c data is reported to the client. The default for the arduino implementation
is 19ms. This means that every 19ms analog data will be reported and
any i2c devices with read continuous mode will be read. Arguments are:;
#X obj 280 1458 cnv 1 38 23 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -245695 -1 0;
#X text 280 1458 TIME: time. Type: int. Range: 10\...10000\. Units:
'ms'.;
